  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\n**Adversarial audit / conditional precision refinement; no new \u03ba.** The retained Gaussian inverse evaluation sums separately rounded powers. Its stated absolute-error interface permits quadratic accumulation even when the exact operator is positive and the approximation is odd and zero-preserving. An all-length exact family establishes that boundary; it does not contradict the existing `3p\u00b2/4` allowance or claim a defect in actual Gaussian rounding.\n\nA fixed-source Horner replacement keeps every intermediate in the disk grid and has error `<p\u00b72^-p`, using exactly the same `k\u22121` complete E calls. The written proof assumes `p>100`, `||E||\u22640.42`, oracle error `<(p/3)2^-p`, and `||E^k||\u22642^-p`. It includes initialization, exact subtraction, residual error, all stream scans and the complete wrapper cost. A separate counterexample shows why merely `||E||<1/2` does not suffice for the disk invariant.\n\nAt p=128 and k=64, the same valid contract fixture gives power-sum error `10528/3` grid units and Horner error `166/3`, with 63 calls each. The old error remains within the old allowance.\n\nOnly `research/neumann-rounding-audit/` is added (eight files). The alternative is implemented at its abstract oracle boundary. Actual Gaussian execution, analytic estimates, PR371's separate block-rounding repair, and physical integration remain open or inherited. No selected supplier, source, precision charge or exponent changes. No benchmark or new mathematical-method priority is claimed.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\n- Research base: `bce54fb3f895cbe5cd4c0eb477c3afeed100190f`; seed **68**, adversarial-audit track; card `uniform-transfer-audit`, scope **refined** to this rounded precision implication.\n- Submission main checked at `410026dc5513b87db92ae98571d1d5984c69a983`: all three consumed source files and selected \u03ba are unchanged. The complete patch applies to that main in a temporary Git index.\n- Exact Git-blob/SHA256 source pins, three candidate tasks, bounded domains, stop rule and next questions are in SOURCES/TASK/VALIDATION. Claim: https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1409.\n- Fresh complete overlap snapshot: 791 open PRs and 148 discussion records. PR684 audits domain/windows, PR902 improves exact-power decay, and PR1243 audits inner packing. This adds rounded-error placement and a source-compatible abstract evaluator. None of those pending implementations is imported. Search coverage is not a novelty proof.\n\n## Validation\n\n```sh\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/neumann-rounding-audit\n```\n\nExpected: `PASS_NEUMANN_ROUNDING_AUDIT fixtures=648 family=326 controls=6`, ten passing tests, then `PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE ... outcome=completed`.\n\nOn macOS arm64 / CPython 3.12.13:\n\n- 648 fixed matrix/oracle cases, all 35,640 states compared between integer and separate Fraction/block-matrix implementations; dense exact elimination supplies the final inverse oracle.\n- 326 complete adverse-family cases through p=1024; six semantic controls cover wrong sign, missing half, omitted tail premise, overwritten source, weakened contraction margin and an unsupported linear bound for the old evaluator.\n- Ten focused tests pass, including source/receipt corruption rejection, input/domain rejection, occupied-output preservation and optimized read-only relocation without Git.\n- Optimized CPython 3.14.6 produces the identical canonical receipt. Selected-record integrity and all five existing selected-result tests pass. Metadata/source pins and whitespace checks pass.\n\nFinite replay is separate from the written universal arguments. No selected cold replay, physical tape compiler execution, full historical suite, hosted-CI success, Lean theorem or independent human review is asserted.\n\n## Credit\n\nCredit eumemic's PR5, icekylinx's retained interfaces, and the Harvey\u2013van der Hoeven resampling lineage; Artus Krohn-Grimberghe's PR371, Effy Elden's PR684, Alan Grillo's PR902 and Hanson's PR1243 are distinct predecessor/context audits with exact heads recorded in the package. Ordinary Horner evaluation and contraction error analysis are standard methods.\n\nPrepared by Hanson Sun (@bbMisk), with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in mathematics, implementation, verification and writing. Apache-2.0; existing sources and notices are preserved.\n\n## Open next questions\n\nThe README and TASK metadata specify two bounded follow-ups: connect the evaluator to an implemented, corrected Gaussian E routine; or derive a stronger actual-rounding property that excludes the adverse family for the original evaluator. The missing integrated routine/analytic adoption and missing stronger error law are explicit blockers. This PR does not perform either integration.\n",
